WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:03.490
Amazon's journey to the Dark Tower is over.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:08.830
Amazon Studios has opted to pass on its planned
adaptation of Stephen King's eight-novel opus

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.929
after reportedly being dissatisfied with the
pilot.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.400
This comes a little more than two years after
the feature film, starring Idris Elba and

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.700
Matthew McConaughey.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.080
The streamer will shop its two completed scripts
to other studios, according to Deadline.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.810
The news comes as a bit of a shock.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.810
King fans were psyched for The Dark Tower
to receive the serial treatment, which would

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.590
have been a great fit for the extremely dense
and profoundly weird material.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.020
The novel series deals with Roland, the last
of a long line of near-mythical Gunslingers,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.140
and his quest to ascend the titular Tower,
which is the nexus of all possible realities.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.329
He's opposed by the mysterious Man in Black,
as well as the Crimson King, an evil extradimensional

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:50.880
entity who has featured directly or indirectly
in several of King's works.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.300
While Amazon had made no official announcements
regarding the series' cast and crew, it had

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.880
been widely reported that the series showrunner
was Glen Mazzara, who had worked on The Walking

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.509
Dead and The Shield; Sam Strike and Jasper
Pääkkönen had been cast as Roland and the

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:08.970
Man in Black, respectively, and Guardians
of the Galaxy's Michael Rooker and Jerome

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:13.270
Flynn from Game of Thrones had also joined
the series in undisclosed roles.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:17.659
Unfortunately, unless the series is picked
up by another network or streamer, Mazzara's

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:20.260
Dark Tower will never see the light of day.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:25.290
Fans who were disappointed by the 2017 feature
film, which attempted to cram several novels'

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:30.110
worth of story into one film and...well, failed,
now have something else to be disappointed

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:31.810
about.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.510
"Jackpot!"

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:37.159
Amazon has made no public statement about
why the plug was pulled on the series, but

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:40.470
Deadline's sources indicate that it wasn't
just one thing.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.240
Of course, as one might have predicted, it
was reported that Mazzara and company were

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.979
having a tough time wrangling the material.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:51.049
What works on the page doesn't always work
on the screen, and the Dark Tower novels serve

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:54.130
as an absolutely splendid illustration of
this truth.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.060
Some of their imagery would be near-impossible
to depict, and some of it, if we're being

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:01.850
honest, would look incredibly silly, no matter
how it was depicted.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:06.290
Aside from these troubles, however, it was
also reported that Amazon's brass simply didn't

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:10.179
feel that the pilot was up to snuff, and that
it would have suffered by comparison with

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:14.560
other fantasy properties the streamer has
cooking, such as Lord of the Rings and The

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.560
Wheel of Time.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.670
While that's certainly a bummer for fans,
there is a silver lining here.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.890
As the 2017 film proved, The Dark Tower is
an extremely easy property to botch, and we

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.450
submit that it's totally possible the powers
that be at Amazon have actually saved us from

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.700
another half-baked adaptation.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:30.700
Who knows?

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.550
As to whether any other brave souls will pick
up the Dark Tower torch, it's tough to say.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:40.150
It's always possible that Mazzara's series
will be rescued by Netflix or HBO, but it

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.500
seems more likely that whatever problems Amazon
had with the pilot won't be overlooked by

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.770
other potentially interested parties.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:51.060
If indeed some intrepid creator decides to
start from scratch on a fresh adaptation,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.061
they would do well to heed the advice of Ron
Howard, who produced the feature film and

00:02:55.061 --> 00:02:59.110
also oversaw a planned tie-in TV series, which
never materialized.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.620
Speaking with Collider last year, Howard indicated
that if he had it to do over again, he would

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.750
have leaned into the weirdness of the source
material rather than trying to shoehorn it

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.740
into a mainstream-friendly package.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.740
He told the outlet,

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.400
"We always felt like we were kind of holding
back something.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.420
Sometimes this happens on these projects where
everybody's best intentions, you're all pulling

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:20.459
in a direction, and then you sort of say,
'Was that the right direction?'

00:03:20.459 --> 00:03:22.690
And I wouldn't say [the movie] was all compromise.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:26.550
I do think it was just a sense of maybe too
much listening to what you think that the

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:31.090
marketplace is calling for instead of the
essence of what Stephen King was giving us."

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.720
Hopefully, one day, we'll get the mind-blowing
serial adaptation that The Dark Tower deserves,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.540
but it likely won't come from Amazon.

